{
 "regions": [
  {
   "id": "r3",
   "type": "stanza_note",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "knowledge of the unbroken and supreme bliss which the Yogis",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "possess, and which is easily attainable by the favour of S'iva.”",
     "end": "join"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "—S'ârdûlavikrîḍita.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "id": "r4",
   "type": "stanza_note",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "St. XXVI.—मृत्युक्षयम् should be मृत्युः क्षयम् as in the Mahânâṭaka",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "p. 153 where this Stanza occurs. The last line is not metrical",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "as it stands. In the Mahânâṭaka it runs thus : चेतः सत्पुरुषाभिमा-",
     "end": "hyphen"
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "नपदवी मिथ्यैव किं खिद्यसे. There are also other differences.—S'ârdû-",
     "end": "hyphen"
    },
    {
     "n": 6,
     "text": "lavikrîḍita.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "id": "r5",
   "type": "stanza_note",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "St. XXVII.—विकल्प = fancies, reveries see note on St. 76.",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "प्रपत्तुम् = to reach, to attain to.—Vans'astha.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "id": "r6",
   "type": "stanza_note",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "St. XXVIII.—तदपि = तथापि, nevertheless. comp. St. 22.—S'i-",
     "end": "hyphen"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "khariṇî.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "id": "r7",
   "type": "stanza_note",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "St. XXIX.—This Stanza is in substance the same as St. 74",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "supra and should have been noted only in the various read-",
     "end": "hyphen"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "ings under that Stanza. भव्य is explained by Râmarshi as श्रेष्ठ or",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "स्वादु. On the first line R. adds आहारस्य गिलितस्यैकरूपत्वादित्यर्थः similar-",
     "end": "hyphen"
    },
    {
     "n": 6,
     "text": "",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 7,
     "text": "ly on the second देहाच्छादनस्यैकरूपत्वात् on the third भोगस्यैकरूपत्वादवसाने",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 8,
     "text": "विरसत्वाच्च on the last देहस्य नश्वरत्वे एकत्वानेकत्वभ्रमणे को विशेषः ॥ एतेन",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 9,
     "text": "रसस्पर्शादयः पदार्थाः सर्वेप्यनित्या इति भावः ॥. —Sragdharâ.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "id": "r8",
   "type": "stanza_note",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "St. XXX.—Anushṭub.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "id": "r9",
   "type": "stanza_note",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "St. XXXI.—अदैन्य = that in which there is no humilia-",
     "end": "hyphen"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "tion or self-abasement. सत्र = पूजन (commentary G.) अवार्य =",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "that from which none can be kept off. अक्षयनिधिम् = अक्षयस्य",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "निधिम् (commentary G.) which is not clear. It means, I think,",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 6,
     "text": "that in which there is an exhaustless treasure. अप्रतिहत is nearly",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 7,
     "text": "the same as अवार्य. N.’s reading is therefore better.—S'ârdûlavi-",
     "end": "hyphen"
    },
    {
     "n": 8,
     "text": "krîḍita.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "id": "r10",
   "type": "stanza_note",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "St. XXXII.—Compare St. 79 supra.—Mandâkrântâ.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "id": "r11",
   "type": "stanza_note",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "St. XXXIII.—तरंगभङ्ग–comp. Prasannarâghava Nâṭaka p. 166.",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "Râmarshi renders भङ्ग apparently by शमन (original शनन) and adds",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "महान्तो हि कल्लोलाः शीघ्रं नश्यन्तीति भावः. The commentary in M. renders",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
